  "query": "Research and map the regulatory and compliance environment for the following:\n\n**Industry:** Medical Devices / MedTech / Continuous Glucose Monitoring, Neurostimulation, Brain-Computer Interface\n**Geography:** North America, Europe (initial); Global (expansion)\n**Problem domain:** LG Innotek (LGIT) has advanced CoF and flexible PCB substrate manufacturing capabilities with 10\u00b5m-level resolution, currently deployed in IT and automotive markets. The company seeks to leverage these capabilities to enter high-value medical device markets\u2014specifically CGM systems, neurostimulation devices, and BCI systems\u2014where thin, flexible, high-density electrode substrates are critical enabling components. The core challenge is determining where in the medical device supply chain LGIT can defensibly participate given its substrate expertise but absence of medical certifications, biosignal IP, and finished-device experience.\n**Solution category:** Advanced Medical Device Substrates, Flexible Circuit Components, and Electrode Modules for Wearable and Implantable Medical Devices\n**Target buyer type:** Enterprise OEM Medical Device Manufacturers\n\nSearch for: \"Medical Devices / MedTech regulations compliance requirements\", \"Medical Devices / MedTech regulatory changes 2025 2026\", \"CoF substrate market entry, flexible circuit medical devices, high-density electrode substrates, implantable device components, wearable sensor modules regulatory requirements\".\n\nResearch and report on:\n\n1. **Current Regulations**: What regulations, standards, and mandates currently affect the problem or solution space? For each, include: name, jurisdiction, key requirements, enforcement status (active/pending/lax), compliance cost if quantified, and source.\n\n2. **Pending Regulatory Changes**: What regulations are proposed, in progress, or expected? Include expected timeline and impact on the venture's problem/solution.\n\n3. **Enforcement Actions**: Recent fines, penalties, or enforcement actions related to non-compliance in this domain. What are the consequences of non-compliance?\n\n4. **Compliance as Buying Friction**: What compliance requirements affect buying decisions for solutions in this category? Security certifications (SOC 2, ISO 27001), data residency, audit requirements? How long do these add to procurement timelines?\n\n5. **Regulatory Urgency Signal**: Is regulation creating urgency to act (mandates with deadlines), or creating friction that slows adoption (complex approval requirements)?\n\n**Named Regulations to Research in Detail:**\n- Research \"ISO 10993 (biocompatibility of medical devices) requirements timeline enforcement\"\n- Research \"ISO 10993 (biocompatibility of medical devices) compliance cost\"\n- Research \"ISO 10993 (biocompatibility of medical devices) penalties non-compliance\"\n- Research \"ISO 13485 (medical device quality management systems) requirements timeline enforcement\"\n- Research \"ISO 13485 (medical device quality management systems) compliance cost\"\n- Research \"ISO 13485 (medical device quality management systems) penalties non-compliance\"\n- Research \"FDA 510(k) clearance requirements timeline enforcement\"\n- Research \"FDA 510(k) clearance compliance cost\"\n- Research \"FDA 510(k) clearance penalties non-compliance\"\n- Research \"FDA PMA (Premarket Approval) requirements timeline enforcement\"\n- Research \"FDA PMA (Premarket Approval) compliance cost\"\n- Research \"FDA PMA (Premarket Approval) penalties non-compliance\"\n- Research \"EU MDR (EU Medical Device Regulation) requirements timeline enforcement\"\n- Research \"EU MDR (EU Medical Device Regulation) compliance cost\"\n- Research \"EU MDR (EU Medical Device Regulation) penalties non-compliance\"\n\n**Compliance Audit Requirements:**\n- Search for \"Medical Devices / MedTech compliance audit requirements frequency\"\n- Search for \"Medical Devices / MedTech compliance technology mandates\"\n\nFor each regulation or standard, cite the specific regulatory body, publication, and date. Distinguish between binding regulations, voluntary standards, and industry best practices.\n\nFocus primarily on North America, Europe (initial); Global (expansion) but note any relevant international standards or regulations from other jurisdictions that influence this market.",
